:''Only a true Dragonborn is worthy.'' &mdash; Official listing

'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a set of items awarded to the [[Lore:Last Dragonborn|Last Dragonborn]] by Jarl [[Lore:Balgruuf the Greater|Balgruuf the Greater]] after slaying the dragon [[Lore:Mirmulnir|Mirmulnir]] during the quest [[Skyrim:Dragon Rising|Dragon Rising]] in ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''. The items are not actually based on a real set of items in game.

{{NewLeft}}

==Description==

Containing the city’s most valuable symbols and treasures, '''{{PAGENAME}}''' has been crafted to bestow the highest honors upon those who have offered exceptional service to the Jarl and the people of Whiterun.

Only a true Dragonborn is worthy of it.

FEATURES & INCLUSIONS

*'''Honorary Citizenship Chest'''
**'''Material:''' Tinplate metal box
**'''Dimensions:''' 10 x 7 in x 2.36 in (25.4 x 17.8 x 6 cm)

*'''Flocking Tray'''
**'''Material:''' Polystyrene with red velvet flocking
**'''Dimensions:''' 10 x 7 in x 2.36 in (25.4 x 17.8 x 6 cm)

*'''Key to the City of Whiterun'''
**'''Material:''' Zinc Alloy
**'''Dimensions:''' 3.94 x 1.42  x 0.51 in (10 x 3.6 x 1.3 cm)

*'''Whiterun Medallion: Balgruuf Necklace'''
**'''Material:''' Zinc Alloy
**'''Dimensions:''' 1.97 x 1.97 x 0.35 in (5 x 5 x 0.9 cm)

*'''Whiterun Banner Flag'''
**'''Material:''' Polyester
**'''Dimensions:''' 53.15 x 17.72 in (135 x 45 cm)

*'''Map of Whiterun'''
**'''Material:''' 120 gsm WF paper
**'''Dimensions:''' 19.29 x 12.99 in (49 x 33 cm) (Folded in two)

*'''[[Lore:Breezehome Certificate of Title|{{sic|Breezehold|Breezehome|nolink=1}} Certificate of Title]]'''
**'''Material:''' 170 gsm WF paper
**'''Dimensions:''' 7.87 x 5.91 in (20 x 15 cm)

*'''[[Lore:Whiterun Hold Jarl's Letter|Whiterun Hold Jarl's Letter]]'''
**'''Material:''' 120 gsm WF paper
**'''Dimensions:''' 8.27 x 11.61  in (21 x 29.5 cm) (Rolled)

*'''Wax Seal (for Jarl’s Letter)'''
**'''Material:''' Wax
**'''Diameter:''' 1.26 in (3.2 cm)
**'''Thickness:''' 0.079 in (0.2 cm)

*'''Commemorative Coin Collection'''
**Three exclusive coins celebrating High King Olaf One-Eye, the hero of Whiterun. 

*'''Ages 14+. This collectible is NOT a toy.'''

